{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-40562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Rounded to two decimal places, what is the acute angle between the vectors $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{8} \\\\ -2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063783/state.json" "file_sha256" "4458209e4a389d6c770550f4bac37c5a801128aad908801ef95ec87361ee35b5"} {"question" "q-40562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{v\\cdot w}{‖v‖\\,‖w‖},\n$$\n\nwe have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{{v}_{1}{w}_{1}+{v}_{2}{w}_{2}+{v}_{3}{w}_{3}+{v}_{4}{w}_{4}}{\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}}\\sqrt{{w}_{1}^{2}+{w}_{2}^{2}+{w}_{3}^{2}+{w}_{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)(4)+(\\sqrt{8})(1)+(-2)(\\sqrt{2})+(-3)(1)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{8})^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-3)^{2}}\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{22}\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{110}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{110}}{220}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{110}}{220})≈{87.27}^{∘}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063783/state.json" "file_sha256" "4458209e4a389d6c770550f4bac37c5a801128aad908801ef95ec87361ee35b5"} {"question" "q-40562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14063783/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "897f5584ea67ca24d20e1e027c055090cd995cc68654d11962ffc41130fab1a3"} {"question" "q-40562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "va